line	<str>If you don't already have raw beef or cooked meat, purchase one from the Nardah General Store.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head west until you reach the River Elid and see an island with lilies growing on it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Attempt to jump to the stepping stones, and throw the meat to the crocodile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick the Lily of the Elid.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back to Zahur.</str>
line	
line	<str>Warm up her chemistry equipment by adjusting the individual heats until the overall temperature is at the marked level.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Zahur to receive the cure crate then bring it to High Priest in Sophanem.</str>
line	
line	<str>Before leaving for the necropolis, gear up for a fight against a level-351 boss using melee equipment.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Go to the <col=800000>necropolis</col> and talk to Maisa, located directly south of the south-eastern gate of Sophanem by the bend in the path.</col>
step	45	-	Quick guide step 45
line	<str>Talk to Jamila in Sophanem (File:Crafting shop icon.png icon on the minimap) to start the quest.</str>
line	
line	<str>Read the message she gives you.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to the campsite, east of Sophanem, directly north of the small mining site by the cliffs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Maisa</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the blocked entry at the Jaltevas Pyramid.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to either a citizen or Menaphite Guard.</str>
line	
line	<str>Fight the Head Menaphite Guard. Do not use Protect from Melee, or he will damage you for 1/3rd of your total hitpoints. Boosting prayers like piety can still be used.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Maisa</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back to Maisa's camp and talk to her.</str>
line	
line	<str>If you need a tinderbox, you can search the camping equipment by the tent to get one. A spade can be found at the north side of the campsite.</str>
line	
line	<str>From the campsite, head south, east around the cliffs, and then north to a set of stairs to the Ruins of Ullek.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the coal and tinderbox on the furnace (marked on the minimap) to ignite it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the well to receive a stone tablet. Read it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head back down the stairs and head south to the southernmost ritual pillar. Dig in front of it (north).</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the chest with the passcode "1118513".</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the furnace with the scarab mould and iron bar, and craft a scarab emblem.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go further north to the pillar, and insert the emblem.</str>
line	
line	<str>Rotate the scarab on the emblem so that it faces downward (pincers facing upward).</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs and defeat the two Scarab Mages. (Logging out will place you outside the cave.)</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down the stairs again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Avoid the projectiles and run west to the junction, south, and east to the lever.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the lever at the end and run as fast as you can back to the junction, then follow the path north and east.</str>
line	
line	<str>At the other end, pull the other lever. If successful, the traps will be disabled.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through the door west of the junction.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the south-western plaque to get four emblems.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the north-western plaque and read it.</str>
line	
line	<str>The solution to the puzzle is different for everyone. Refer to the table below to solve this puzzle.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pull the lever to the south-west and continue to the next area.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to the Spirit.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the rusty key from the urn in the back of the room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Prepare for the next boss fight, who is best fought with ranged. Resupply now if necessary. (Make sure to bring the rusty key, the fight begins immediately after unlocking the door.)</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the room where you faced the Scarab Mages, and open the door (it only needs to be unlocked once).</str>
line	
line	<str>Defeat the Champion of Scabaras. It will attack with magic, or melee when next to the player. It is recommended to use Protect from Magic and stay out of melee range of the boss. After several normal attacks, it will use one of three special attacks.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the High Priest of Scabaras.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to Nardah and talk to Maisa or Zahur in the building directly south of the fountain.</str>
line	
line	<str>If you don't already have raw beef or cooked meat, purchase one from the Nardah General Store.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head west until you reach the River Elid and see an island with lilies growing on it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Attempt to jump to the stepping stones, and throw the meat to the crocodile.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick the Lily of the Elid.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go back to Zahur.</str>
line	
line	<str>Warm up her chemistry equipment by adjusting the individual heats until the overall temperature is at the marked level.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Zahur to receive the cure crate then bring it to High Priest in Sophanem.</str>
line	
line	<str>Before leaving for the necropolis, gear up for a fight against a level-351 boss using melee equipment.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the necropolis and talk to Maisa, located directly south of the south-eastern gate of Sophanem by the bend in the path.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>At the end of the cutscene, defeat the <col=800000>Menaphite Akh</col>. The Menaphite Akh attacks using melee, and will occasionally use special attacks.</col>
